list.item:
Anderson, Dillon, Special Assistant to the
                        President for National Security Affairs, April 2, 1955–September 1, 1956;
                        White House Consultant from June 29, 1957

Gray, Gordon, Assistant Secretary of Defense
                        for International Security Affairs, July 14, 1955-February 27, 1957;
                        Director, Office of Defense Mobilization from March 4, 1957

Herrera Palacios, Oscar, Chilean Minister of
                        Education, January-August, 1955; Minister of Economy, August-October 1955;
                        Minister of Finance and Economy, October 1955-August 1956

Kreiger Vasena, Adalberto, member of the
                        Argentine Financial Mission to the United States, June-September 1956;
                        Argentine Minister of Finance from March 1957

McGuire, E. Perkins, Deputy Assistant Secretary
                        of Defense for International Security Affairs, January-December 1956;
                        thereafter, Assistant Secretary of Defense for Supply and Logistics

Rojas, Rear Admiral Isaac Francisco,
                        Provisional Vice President of Argentina, September 25-November 13, 1955;
                        thereafter, Vice President and member of the Junta

person.note:
Under Secretary of the Treasury for Monetary Affairs until September 26, 1957;
                    thereafter, U.S. Permanent Representative to the North Atlantic Treaty
                    Organization

Deputy Assistant Secretary of State for Economic Affairs until March 14, 1957;
                    Assistant Secretary of State for Economic Affairs, March 15-September 26, 1957;
                    Ambassador to El Salvador from December 6, 1957

Counselor, Embassy in Guatemala, September 16, 1954-November 24, 1955;
                    Ambassador to El Salvador, November 24, 1955-September 24, 1957; Assistant
                    Secretary of State for Economic Affairs from September 30, 1957

Assistant Secretary of the Army for Financial Management until 1955, and again
                    from 1957; Assistant Secretary of the Army for Civil-Military Affairs,
                    1955–1957

Director, Executive Secretariat, Department of State, until August 1, 1955;
                    thereafter, Deputy Director for Management, International Cooperation
                    Administration

First Secretary and Counselor, Embassy in Argentina, until January 15, 1956;
                    Office of South American Affairs, Department of State, January 15–30, 1956;
                    Officer in Charge of West Coast Affairs, January 30-November 4, 1956,
                    thereafter, Officer in Charge of Brazilian Affairs

Colombian Ambassador to the United Nations until September 1957;
                    Representative to the Security Council, 1957; President of that Council, August
                    1957; Ambassador to the United States, November 10, 1955-September 1957

Second Secretary and Consul, Embassy in Argentina until September 11, 1955;
                    thereafter, Office of South American Affairs, Bureau of Inter-American Affairs,
                    Department of State

Assistant Secretary of State for Economic Affairs until August 25, 1955;
                    Deputy Under Secretary of State for Economic Affairs, August 26-October 1, 1955;
                    President and Chairman of the Board of Directors, Export-Import Bank, from
                    October 4, 1955
